From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 22:49:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] engine: translate profile settings into ghostty's config

Wires PLAN's five MVP fields now that ghostty_config_set exists: font
face and size, scrollback (WT counts lines; a negative historySize means
infinite, which is ghostty's default, so it is left unset), the colour
scheme including all 16 palette entries, and padding.

Padding is set to zero deliberately. WT already insets the
SwapChainPanel by the profile's padding, so asking ghostty to pad as well
would double it - and until the colours matched, WT's padding was drawn
in the profile's background while the pane was drawn in ghostty's,
which is what made it look like a border round the terminal.

Two things this needed that were not obvious:

- A surface is born with the *app's* config. The first version built a
  config, translated into it, and never applied it - a silent no-op, and
  the pane came up correct in every respect except that it ignored every
  setting. ghostty_surface_update_config is what applies it.

- Parsing config entries overflows WT's 1 MB UI thread stack, the same
  way bringing the engine up did. Rather than fix the one call site,
  GhosttyEngine::RunWithEngineStack now exists so that anything touching
  libghostty deeply runs where it has room, and the constraint has one
  documented home instead of being rediscovered as a crash.

Also adds OutputDebugString tracing of the entries applied, the cell
size, the pushed surface size and connection resizes. A packaged app has
no stdout, and every sizing bug in this phase was invisible from outside;
these are what turned the last one from guesswork into arithmetic.

Verified from the traces: font-family "Cascadia Mono", font-size 12,
scrollback 9001, background #0c0c0c and the full Campbell palette all
accepted, cellSize 14x28, surface 1682x840, grid 119x29.

